# The menu (SUPER+Space). One item per line:
#   group | title | description | command | glyph (top level only, one character)
# A line with an empty title describes its group: description, glyph, and a
# generated list (menu: …) if it has one. A top-level item has an empty group.
# The top level is always Apps, Keybinds, Style, Setup, Capture, Install,
# Remove, Update and System, in that order; other groups follow them.
# Commands run detached. Prefixes:
#   term:      run in a terminal, which stays open at a prompt afterwards
#   menu:      a generated list (apps, keys, install, remove, theme, terminal,
#              agent), or "menu: list <command>" for the lines of
#              `@DISTRO_ID@ <command> menu-items`
# Copy this file to ~/.config/@DISTRO_ID@/menu to change your own. Older copies
# still work: Learn and Power items show under System, Toggle under Setup.

Apps     | | launch anything        | menu: apps    | ◆
Keybinds | | learn and edit         | menu: keys    | ?
Style    | | theme, wallpaper, bar  |               | ◐
Setup    | | wi-fi, displays, audio |               | ~
Capture  | | screenshot, record     |               | ◎
Install  | | apps and packages      | menu: install | +
Remove   | |                        | menu: remove  | −
| Update | | term: @DISTRO_ID@ update | ↑
System   | | lock, reboot, power off |              | !
| Coding agent | SUPER+A | @DISTRO_ID@ agent open | ◇

